{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01296","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01296@rel:R19-11#f4c8360b","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01296","release":"R19-11","content":"Different approaches of ASAM MCD-2MC and AUTOSAR with respect to SwRecordLayout ASAM MCD-2D specification (also known as 443 of 1124  AUTOSAR CONFIDENTIAL  Document ID 62: AUTOSAR_TPS_SoftwareComponentTemplate Software Component Template AUTOSAR CP R19-11 A2L, or ASAP) uses keywords in record layouts where MSR/AUTOSAR uses the more generic approach specified here. It may happen that this generic approach cannot always be safely mapped to the A2L keywords. Therefore, SwRecordLayoutV . category as well as SwRecordLayout- Group . category can assist the conversion to the current A2L format.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_TPS_SoftwareComponentTemplate.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:25+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01296@rel:R20-11#26277907","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01296","release":"R20-11","content":"Different approaches of ASAM MCD-2MC and AUTOSAR with respect to SwRecordLayout ASAM MCD-2D specification (also known as 435 of 1113 Document ID 62: AUTOSAR_TPS_SoftwareComponentTemplate Software Component Template AUTOSAR CP R20-11 A2L, or ASAP) uses keywords in record layouts where MSR/AUTOSAR uses the more generic approach specified here. It may happen that this generic approach cannot always be safely mapped to the A2L keywords. Therefore, SwRecordLayoutV . category as well as SwRecordLayout- Group . category can assist the conversion to the current A2L format.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_TPS_SoftwareComponentTemplate.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:45+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01296@rel:R25-11#9322d5e7","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/TPS_SWCT_01296","release":"R25-11","content":"Different appro